<title>USA: BPA says it offering no energy for Weds delivery.</title>
<headline>BPA says it offering no energy for Weds delivery.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) said it was offering no energy for delivery Wednesday, August 6.</p>
<p>BPA on Monday had offered power at $25.00 per megawatt hour (MWh) for Northwest sales and $26.00 for California-Oregon border (COB) sales for Tuesday delivery.</p>
<p>The agency offered only 200 megawatts for Tuesday sales.</p>
<p>((--Chris Reese, New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627))</p>
